From 678c4832e5857ff28c02f64f9967f3abdaf78567 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:18:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(post): Fanuc-family mill posts state the clearance Z
 before the first X/Y traverse

fanuc, haas, mazak, doosan-dnm, sinumerik and heidenhain wrote the first
move after a tool change as one combined rapid (G00 X20 Y10 Z-3) from
wherever the change left the tip - a straight line through the part when a
long tool on a high work offset stands below the part top (the #1614
hazard). At the program's start and after every tool change the first
motion now starts with a Z-only rapid to the section's ClearancePlane, else
its RetractPlane, never below the move's own Z, then X/Y alone at it (and,
for a feed, arc or probing move, a rapid down to its start). A first canned
cycle is positioned over its hole at that height. A stream stating neither
plane is refused by name with the #1618/#1632 wording.

Frame: written after the record's own tilt(), so under G43.4 when the first
record arms it (the tip's work-frame Z) and in G43 with the table clamped on
Doosan's indexing path; the rotaries turn only on the record. Decision in
docs/decisions/1633-fanuc-first-traverse-clearance.md.

Pinned by crates/post/tests/first_traverse_clearance_fanuc_family.rs; 161
goldens gained only the inserted Z (and X/Y) rapids, checked by script.

Fixes #1633
Refs #1616

